Inspect the notification targets of the server (the notify_* subsystems of the
configuration, see "nexoctl admin config set"): their ARN for "nexoctl event
add", their state and the events waiting in their queue on the answering node.

Usage:
  nexoctl admin notify [flags]
  nexoctl admin notify [command]

Available Commands:
  targets     List and test the notification targets

Flags:
  -h, --help   help for notify

Global Flags:
      --config-dir string   configuration directory (default $NEXOCTL_CONFIG_DIR or ~/.nexoctl)
      --debug               dump the HTTP requests and responses on stderr, with the secrets redacted
      --json                print JSON Lines (one object per line with a "status" member)
      --no-color            disable colors (also with the NO_COLOR environment variable)
  -q, --quiet               hide confirmations and progress (results and errors are still printed)

Use "nexoctl admin notify [command] --help" for more information about a command.
